{
  "description": "Shared webhook signature test vectors for the Soroban Pulse SDKs. Scheme (docs/webhook_signing.md): header X-Signature-256 = 'sha256=' + lowercase hex HMAC-SHA256(secret, raw body). When timestamps are enabled the signed message is '<timestamp>.<raw body>' and the timestamp is sent in X-Signature-Timestamp (unix seconds). A request is valid if the signature matches any of the listed secrets (rotation) and, when a timestamp is present, it is within the tolerance window. 'error' is the expected failure class: missing, format, mismatch or expired. All signatures below are real HMAC-SHA256 digests of the given payload/secret and can be recomputed by any SDK.",
